  "Time alignment does not make these the same measurement: retail electricity purchases are not total electricity consumption, and an output index is not kilowatthours.",
  "G.17 rates are seasonally adjusted; the EIA retail sales are not. Comparing the same quarter or month of consecutive years limits seasonal differences but does not remove weather or calendar differences.",
  "The sources are different vintages: each G.17 value is as printed in the release named beside it, and the EIA file is one retrieval whose edition is not stated. They are not a common historical information set.",
  "Whether the Federal Reserve's output measures draw on EIA data is not stated in the retained material, so the two sources are not treated as independent: agreement between them is not corroboration.",
  "Observed periods only. They neither validate nor invalidate either series as a general guide to the other, and no cause is established."
